  "description": "the CLASS RULE construction 'every cat is an animal.' - an explicit rule that one class is contained in another. Pattern order: literal 'every', NP:sub (bare noun), literal 'is', NPIND:sup (an NPIND slot matches 'a NOUN' or 'an NOUN' - the indefinite article plus a noun, as ONE slot; do NOT write 'a' or 'an' as separate literals). Meaning: frame 'class_rule' with sub @sub and sup @sup - no tense, no polarity. For counterexamples give word-ORDER-scrambled strings like 'every is cat an animal.' - note that plural nouns like cats still parse, so changing a noun is NOT a broken string",
  "shape_hint": "every cat is an animal.",
  "surface_meta": {
   "mood": "declarative"
  },
  "scaffold_semantics": {
   "frame": "class_rule",
   "sub": "@sub",
   "sup": "@sup"
  },
  "example_sentence_hint": "shaped 'every cat is an animal.' (nouns include: cat, dog, animal, creature, milo)",
